{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability) in each lottery. In Lottery A, no outcome occurs with 100% probability: the highest probability is 66% for 2400 Euros. In contrast, Lottery B offers 2400 Euros with 100% probability, making it a sure outcome. Therefore, the decision reason can be applied: Lottery B has a sure outcome, Lottery A does not. The reason would prefer Lottery B due to the presence of a sure outcome.",
