  "step_3": "The decision reason hinges on the presence of a sure outcome, but neither lottery has one, so the reason would not lead to a preference in this case. Moreover, the individual did not consider certainty or the structure of probabilities; instead, they focused only on the monetary amounts. There is no indication that the individual evaluated whether an outcome was certain in either lottery. Therefore, the information relevant to the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome) was not considered, and the individual’s justification (based on money amount) does not align with the rule of the reason (preference for a sure outcome).",
